# Changelog

To install the unreleased climux version, see [developmental releases](https://climux.git-pull.com/quickstart.html#developmental-releases).

[pip](https://pip.pypa.io/en/stable/):

```console
$ pip install --user --upgrade --pre climux
```

[uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/):

```console
$ uv add climux --prerelease allow
```

## climux 0.0.0 (unreleased)

<!-- KEEP THIS PLACEHOLDER - DO NOT REMOVE OR MODIFY THIS LINE -->
_Notes on the upcoming release will go here._
<!-- END PLACEHOLDER - ADD NEW CHANGELOG ENTRIES BELOW THIS LINE -->

### Documentation

#### Process and log fields are documented (#4)

The dataclasses describing managed processes, their configuration, and
captured log entries now say what each field holds.

### Development

#### Lint floor moved to ruff 0.16 (#5)

Minimum `ruff>=0.16.0` (was unpinned). Contributors now get one shared set
of diagnostics rather than whatever ruff their machine resolved.

`ruff format` reaches the Python samples inside `README.md` and `AGENTS.md`
in addition to the source tree, so documentation code blocks stay in step
with the code they illustrate.

#### ruff's default rule set is now in force (#5)

ruff 0.16 ships a curated default rule set, and naming rules under `select`
opts a project out of it entirely. Lint configuration now layers this
project's own linters on top of those defaults, so contributors see the
diagnostics ruff treats as its baseline alongside the ones this project
picked.

Everything the wider set surfaced is fixed in the source rather than muted.
The exceptions are the blind `except` handlers and the silent
`try`/`except`/`pass` paths on the process-supervision and JSON-RPC
boundaries, which carry per-file ignores in `pyproject.toml` next to the
reason each one is deliberate.

